kind check-if
title Check if activating a font file would change anything.
intro `vtium-config activate --dry-run` says what `vtium-config activate` would add to the draft's active fonts, and saves nothing.
see fonts/use-a-font-file-that-is-not-active
waits-for audit 11: `activate --dry-run` prints what `activate` prints

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
font fonts/wide.bdf 10x20

1. Press q to quit.
2. Run `vtium-config activate ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf --dry-run`.
at the dry run
check said shows "wide.bdf"
check said shows "nothing was saved"
